.Dd July 11, 2022
.Dt ZPOOL-SYNC 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zpool-sync
.Nd flush data to primary storage of ZFS storage pools
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm zpool
.Cm sync
.Op Fl l
.Oo Ar pool Oc Ns …
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command forces all in-core dirty data to be written to the primary
pool storage and not the ZIL.
It will also update administrative information including quota reporting.
Without arguments,
.Nm zpool Cm sync
will sync all pools on the system.
Otherwise, it will sync only the specified pools.
For a pool with an asynchronous mirror, the command then waits until the
lagging child has applied the transaction group that the command synced.
For other pools, the command returns as soon as the transaction group syncs.
Only the
.Nm zpool Cm sync
process waits; the pool's sync thread and application writes do not wait for
the lagging child.
.
.Pp
If the lagging child is frozen, failed, switched off, switching off, or its
copy is suspended, the command writes a message to standard error and returns
status 0.
The sync itself succeeded on the leader.
If a signal interrupts the wait, the command returns a nonzero status.
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l
Leader only.
Return when the transaction group has synced to the leader.
Do not wait for the lagging child.
This is the behavior used by earlier versions of this command.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zpoolconcepts 7 ,
.Xr zpool-export 8 ,
.Xr zpool-iostat 8
